n money  his accusers accepted his denial and the  business was hushed up however Monroe  sent incriminating copies of the letters  between Reynolds and Hamilton to his  close ally and Hamilton's arch enemy  Thomas Jefferson five years later in  1797 James Callender  at that time a propagandist for  Jefferson made the made the affair  public in a pamphlet Hamilton angrily  confronted Monroe for betraying him  words were exchanged each called the  other a scoundrel and a liar a duel  between the two was only narrowly  averted through the efforts of none  other than Aaron Burr though of course  would himself kill Hamilton and a duel  in 1804 can't make it up by this time  the reynolds affair was public knowledge  a major embarrassment to Hamilton and  one of several factors that denied him  any further role in public office he  published a 95 page pamphlet in his  defense in which he admitted to the  affair in great detail apologized for it  and once again denied that he had done  anything corrupt in his role as Treasury  secretary although Hamilton remained  high in the esteem of George Washington  his reputation was permanently tarnished  less however for his sexual  improprieties than for succumbing to  bribery and for his concealment of it  which fed into a wide perception among  Jeffersonian Democrats and some of his  fellow Federalists that Hamilton was a  man who just couldn't be trusted  the propagandist James Callender was  also a pivotal figure in what today is  doubtless the most famous scandal of the  era after two centuries of denial by  Thomas Jefferson's white descendants  virtually all historians now accept that  he kept an enslaved negro concubine with  whom he had sexual relations for decades  and produced several children salacious  allusions to dusky Sally were part and  parcel of what might be termed America's  first golden age of scandal mongering  they were a coda to the fiercely  contested election of 1800 which was one  of the dirtiest in American history  right up to our own time and I think a  case could be made that it was by far  the dirtiest frankly that election  represented the first handover of power  from one hostile political party to  another from Federalists to Democratic  Republicans an unprecedented experience  that encouraged candidates to demonize  the opposition as satanic threats rather  than to regard them as worthy and  principled competitors sound familiar if  you think that today's press by the way  is too partisan you should read the  newspapers of the 1800 the aurora for  example when there was no such thing as  fair and balanced coverage of anything  Jefferson's Republicans Democrat  Republicans formally accused Federalists  Adams of insanity senility plotting to  establish a monarchy hatred of the  people collusion with Britain against  American interests and of having a  hideous hermaphroditical character  you know take that the Federalists  accused Jefferson of having cheated his  law clients showing cowardice in the  face of the enemy during the Revolution  atheism and being head of the French  party in America one partisan journalist  predicted that if Jefferson were to be  elected licentiousness and immorality  would meet with the most public  approbation every restraint would soon  be thrown off and men would soon bring  themselves to be infamous debo Shay's  assassins cheats thieves liars  hateful and hating one another a curse  upon the earth 1800  so the accusation against Jefferson of  miscegenation was thus but once girl is  charged among many there had been rumors  for some time that Jefferson was  carrying on a liaison with an enslaved  woman then in 1802 the hints became  explicit when the pamphleteer James  Callender now a renegade former  supporter of Jefferson wrote in the  richmond recorder it is well known that  the man who matt delighteth the people  to honor keeps and for many years past  has kept as his concubine one of his own  slaves her name is Sally  th